// boss. ADMINS is the opt-in for genuine institute-ops obligations (the\n/// electricity bill, the rent) that the owner also needs to see.\nenum ReminderAudience {\n  PRIVATE\n  ADMINS\n}\n\n/// A dated obligation that notifies its audience `leadDays` before it's due.\n/// Distinct from `POST /org/reminders`, which broadcasts an ad-hoc message\n/// to team roles *immediately* and stores nothing — this one is scheduled,\n/// persistent, and optionally recurring. Fired by services/reminderScheduler.ts\n/// (in-process ticker started in server.ts). See changes-phase8.md §8d.\nmodel ScheduledReminder {\n  id              String           @id @default(cuid())\n  instituteId     String\n  createdByUserId String\n  title           String\n  category        ReminderCategory @default(OTHER)\n  /// The date the thing is actually due. For a repeating reminder this is\n  /// always the *next* occurrence — the scheduler rolls it forward once the\n  /// date has passed, rather than storing one row per cycle.\n  dueDate         DateTime         @db.Date\n  /// Every lead time this reminder notifies at, in days before `dueDate` —\n  /// e.g. [90, 30, 15, 7, 1] pings four times as a deadline approaches. Plain\n  /// Ints rather than an enum so the common presets and any custom number are\n  /// the same thing. Stored sorted descending (earliest notification first).\n  leadDays        Int[]\n  repeat          ReminderRepeat   @default(NONE)\n  audience        ReminderAudience @default(PRIVATE)\n  notes           String?\n  isActive        Boolean          @default(true)\n  /// Display only — \"last notified on\".\n  lastFiredAt     DateTime?\n\n  // --- Scheduler cursor -----------------------------------------------------\n  // Together these answer \"when does this next need to notify, and for which\n  // lead time?\" without the scheduler having to compute anything per row.\n  // Both are derived from dueDate + leadDays and are always rewritten in the\n  // same operation as thos